&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us in designing the future of grocery shopping. As a Product Designer in our consumer team, you&#39;ll own the design of our core mobile app, shaping the daily shopping experience for hundreds of thousands of people in The Netherlands, Germany and France. You&#39;ll tackle the unique challenge of designing for a task that is frequent, personal, and central to our customers&#39; lives. You&#39;ll be part of a dedicated product team and our wider UX Guild, a creative community that ensures a world-class user experience across Picnic. We’re looking for a passionate designer to join our Amsterdam HQ and help build a product people genuinely love, in a fast-scaling environment that values autonomy, collaboration, and adaptability over rigid processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the autonomy to own the design of new features from beginning to end. Everything you do matters and will be developed and tested at a fast pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sharpen project briefs based on explorative research together with UX researchers and product owners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build low and high fidelity prototypes to be tested and evaluated on a weekly basis with real users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document the final design requirements on interaction and UI level to brief and support developers during the development phase.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow through the continuous feedback and mentoring by seasoned UX designers and researchers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and maintenance of our design libraries and system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously explore new ideas in order to initiate new projects and improvements, design is never done ;).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your superpowers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-list-tree=&quot;true&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You have a completed degree in a relevant design field (e.g. CMD, UX, Interaction or Product Design)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You have 0-3 years of experience as a UX designer and have worked on or have a strong interest in building great products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Your portfolio has user-centered design cases that show your problem solving capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You have a deep curiosity to understand our customers and have hands-on experience in exploratory research to discover and define user problems from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You know your way around Figma and are able to craft high-fidelity designs that fit into our design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;You bring a low-ego, collaborative mindset and enjoy building solutions together&lt;/li&gt;
